  "response": "To tell `promptfoo scan-model` which registry URI to use for JFrog or MLflow, you need to specify the model path in the command. Here's how you can do it based on the context provided:\n\n### JFrog Artifactory\n\nWhen scanning a model from JFrog Artifactory, you need to specify the complete URL to the model file:\n\n```bash\n# Scan from JFrog Artifactory\npromptfoo scan-model \"https://your-domain.jfrog.io/artifactory/models/model.pkl\"\n```\n\nMake sure to replace `your-domain.jfrog.io` and the path `models/model.pkl` with your actual JFrog Artifactory domain and model path.\n\n### MLflow Model Registry\n\nFor MLflow, you must provide the model registry path in the format `models:/ModelName/Version` or `models:/ModelName/Latest`. Before running the scan, ensure you have set the necessary MLflow tracking environment variables:\n\n```bash\n# Authenticate with MLflow\nexport MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=\"https://your-mlflow-server.com\"\nexport MLFLOW_TRACKING_USERNAME=\"your-username\"\nexport MLFLOW_TRACKING_PASSWORD=\"your-password\"\n\n# Scan from MLflow\npromptfoo scan-model models:/MyModel/Latest\n```\n\nReplace `https://your-mlflow-server.com`, `your-username`, `your-password`, `MyModel`, and `Latest` with your specific MLflow server details and model information.\n\nThese commands use the appropriate URIs or paths to access the models stored in JFrog Artifactory and MLflow, respectively.",
